Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TicketLens vendors no third-party source code. It installs the following
separately licensed packages at setup time; each retains its own copyright and
license terms. Licenses below were read from the installed package metadata of
the tested environment (see requirements.txt for the pinned versions).

  bertopic .................. MIT
  umap-learn ................ BSD-3-Clause
  hdbscan ................... BSD-3-Clause
  scikit-learn .............. BSD-3-Clause
  numba ..................... BSD-2-Clause
  numpy ..................... BSD-3-Clause AND 0BSD AND MIT AND Zlib AND CC0-1.0
  sentence-transformers ..... Apache-2.0
  llama-cpp-python .......... MIT
  pandas .................... BSD-3-Clause
  openpyxl .................. MIT
  PySide6 ................... LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only
  matplotlib ................ Python Software Foundation License (BSD-compatible)
  plotly .................... MIT
  kaleido ................... MIT
  wordcloud ................. MIT
  python-docx ............... MIT
  Jinja2 .................... BSD-3-Clause

Optional, installed only by install_openvino.bat:

  openvino, openvino-tokenizers, nncf, onnx ... Apache-2.0
  datasets .................................... Apache-2.0

Optional, installed only by install_mlx.sh (Apple Silicon):

  mlx ......................................... MIT
  mlx-lm ...................................... MIT
  mlx-embeddings .............................. GPL-3.0   <-- note the difference

IMPORTANT -- mlx-embeddings is GPL-3.0, unlike everything else listed here.
TicketLens does not bundle, vendor or redistribute it: it is fetched from PyPI
by install_mlx.sh only if you choose to run that script, and the app is fully
functional without it. Apache-2.0 and GPL-3.0 are one-way compatible (Apache-2.0
code may be combined into a GPL-3.0 work, not the reverse), so if YOU distribute
a bundle that includes mlx-embeddings, that combined distribution must comply
with GPL-3.0. If you would rather avoid this entirely, do not run
install_mlx.sh: the Apple GPU is still used for embeddings through PyTorch MPS
(BSD-3-Clause) and for LLM labelling through the Metal llama.cpp build (MIT).

Note on PySide6/Qt: TicketLens links PySide6 dynamically and does not
redistribute it. If you build and ship a bundled binary that embeds Qt, the
LGPL-3.0 relinking obligations apply to your distribution.

